From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 03:47:22 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] watchdog: pm8916_wdt: drop a pretimeout that no longer fits
 the timeout

The bark (S1) timer is programmed as timeout - pretimeout. When the
timeout is set at or below the current pretimeout, that subtraction
underflows, and the 8-bit register gets whatever the low bits are. The
watchdog core drops such a pretimeout itself, but only for drivers without
a set_timeout callback, and this driver has one.

Drop the pretimeout in that case, as the core does.

Fixes: 969c0acc039f ("watchdog: Add pm8916 watchdog driver")
Signed-off-by: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
---
 drivers/watchdog/pm8916_wdt.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/watchdog/pm8916_wdt.c b/drivers/watchdog/pm8916_wdt.c
index 007ed139ab..b227a9dde1 100644
--- a/drivers/watchdog/pm8916_wdt.c
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/pm8916_wdt.c
@@ -88,6 +88,9 @@ static int pm8916_wdt_set_timeout(struct watchdog_device *wdev,
 				  unsigned int timeout)
 {
 	wdev->timeout = timeout;
+	/* Disable pretimeout if it doesn't fit the new timeout */
+	if (wdev->pretimeout >= wdev->timeout)
+		wdev->pretimeout = 0;
 
 	return pm8916_wdt_configure_timers(wdev);
 }
